findings.citation_text:
4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) between soft serve machine and drive thru reach-in cooler (splash);
B) inside apple pie cooler (debris/moisture);
C) reach-in freezer across from pie cooler (food debris);  
D) storage cabinet at frozen Fanta machine (sticky buildup);
E) bun storage rack at end of make line (general buildup); and
F) fryer lid storage cubby on make line (grease).
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.

findings.comment:
750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) salad cooler - ledge beneath condenser in bottom of unit (food debris);
B) cook line reach-in freezer - bottom inside (crumbs);
C) ice scoop at main ice machine - handle and top edge of holder (general buildup);
D) inside cabinets at lobby soda counter (general buildup);
E) cup storage on side of shake machine (general buildup);
F) frappe/smoothie blender base (food splash);
G) shake cup holders (splash);   and
H) frozen Coke machine - inside syrup storage compartment (syrup splash/buildup).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
